# KNOWN GAP (ASan lane). The value-lane twin is
# tests/fixtures/known_gaps/shared_plain_call_param_uaf.gg — same program, different lane.
# reads freed memory (rc -11 / 139; ASan `heap-use-after-free`).
#
# A `Shared[T]` passed to a plain function is BORROWED. AGENTS.md § "Ownership at
# Consuming Positions" says so explicitly of the single-owner-by-design family:
# *"At a plain function / method call these types are simply borrowed, so no
# operator is needed."* The caller keeps its handle. It does not:
#
#   ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free
#       #0 gorget_shared_get_ptr  #1 Shared__int64_t__get  #2 main
#   freed by:
#       gorget_shared_drop ← Shared__int64_t__drop ← read_it
#
# — the CALLEE decrefs at scope exit and frees the cell under the caller. Root
# cause is filed: `needs_param_drop` (`src/ir/types.rs:602`) keys on TYPE only and
# cannot tell bare `Shared s` (borrow) from `Shared !s` (owned). See todo/t0108,
# which this cell is evidence for — it is NOT a separate defect.
#
# ⭐ THE SELF-HOST LANE IS CORRECT HERE, so it is the ORACLE: fix the Rust side,
# never dumb the self-host down to match (AGENTS.md, the succession plan).
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the wired test): prints 42 twice.
# Evidence added 2026-08-30 by R47 Track F4a.

int read_it(Shared[int] s):
    return s.get()


void main():
    Shared[int] s = Shared[int](42)
    print(f"{read_it(s)}")
    print(f"{s.get()}")
